course: dictionary
lesson: 13157
title: Formality: rules, steps and manners
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A formality is a step that must be done because of rules or custom. Often it changes nothing. «Signing the form was just a formality» means the result was already certain, so the signing was only a required step.
explain: Formality can also mean polite, stiff behaviour. «The formality of the banquet made Sam sit up straight and use the correct fork.» The clue is the careful, correct manners, not paperwork.
explain: Look for clue words. Just, only and mere point to a step that changes nothing. Legal, official and border point to paperwork. Ask yourself: is this a rule-step, or is it about stiff manners? Then swap in your meaning and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: A formality is an official step or a stiff, polite way of behaving.
fact: «A mere formality» means something that is sure to happen anyway.
fact: «Formalities» (plural) are official steps, such as signing forms at a border.
fact: «Without formality» means relaxed and friendly, with no stiff rules.
fact: Formality is a noun, and it comes from the word formal, which means following set rules or customs.
exercise: «Showing your passport at the airport desk was just a formality.» What does formality mean here? | *A step that must be done, though it changes nothing | A type of weather | A dance at a party | A loud argument
exercise: «Everyone wore smart clothes and spoke in careful, polite voices, because the formality of the ceremony was strict.» What does formality mean here? | Heavy rain on the roof | *Stiff, polite and correct behaviour | Messy play in the garden | A small pet
exercise: «The boat could not leave until the forms were signed, so there were many legal formalities.» What are the formalities? | Sleepy animals below deck | Tasty snacks for the crew | *Official steps needed because of rules | Games played on the deck
test: «It is only a formality: the match is sure to go ahead.» What does only a formality suggest? | Nobody knows what will happen | The match is cancelled | The referee is angry | *The outcome is certain
test: «Cara went through the border formalities with her passport and a stamp.» Which of these is a formality? | Singing a song loudly | *Showing a passport and getting a stamp | Eating a sandwich in the rain | Swimming in a lake
exam: «The party was held without formality, so the children wore jeans and ran about.» What does without formality mean? | Without any food | *Relaxed, with no stiff rules or manners | With a long speech | With strict rules on every step
